            <ArticleTitle>A versatile route to polythiophenes with functional pendant groups using alkyne chemistry.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2682-2688</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3762/bjoc.12.265</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new versatile polythiophene building block, 3-(3,4-ethylenedioxythiophene)prop-1-yne (pyEDOT) (3), is prepared from glycidol in four steps in 28% overall yield. pyEDOT features an ethynyl group on its ethylenedioxy bridge, allowing further functionalization by alkyne chemistry. Its usefulness is demonstrated by a series of functionalized polythiophene derivatives that were obtained by pre- and post-electropolymerization transformations, provided by the synthetic ease of the Sonogashira coupling and click chemistry.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
